      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould you check what dose you intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg per day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg per day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg per day.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a reason for the order note."
      }
